From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Frost is the smoked glass on the shelf and its
 pop-overs

Studio Desktop's approved Frost is a smoked glass with dark ink in Light and
Dark alike: the islands take the glass gradient from rgba(40,40,45,.74) to
rgba(26,26,30,.84) and pop-overs the denser rgba(50,50,56,.8) to
rgba(32,32,36,.86), both over a blur of 40 at saturation 1.4, with a bright
top edge and a faint rim. Frost surfaces now wear the dark family's classes
plus luma-surface-smoke, so their ink, wells and marks are the dark ones;
application windows keep the platform Frost recipe.

